//! Inputs: what an instance's flight recorder holds of each input its handler calls took.

/// The header of an input as a flight recorder holds it: its number, increasing over the instance's incarnations in a boot, the monotonic time its handler call began, its cause as a header holds it, the XXH3-64 of its encoding and its bytes, both 0 when it moved without one, the slot of its sender, 0 for the core, its handler call's run time in µs, saturating, its operation's number, its flags, and its outcome, one of [InputOutcome].
pub layout InputHeader: bytes 48 le {
    seq: u64 at 0
    time: u64 at 8
    cause: u64 at 16
    hash: u64 at 24
    sender: u32 at 32
    size: u32 at 36
    run_us: u32 at 40
    operation: u8 at 44
    flags: InputFlags at 45
    outcome: u8 at 46
    reserved: u8 at 47
} InputHeader

/// The flags of an input: a request, an encoded payload, a dead letter delivered again, a system interface call.
pub layout InputFlags: u8 {
    request: bit 0
    encoded: bit 1
    redelivered: bit 2
    system: bit 3
    reserved: rest
} InputFlags

/// The outcome of an input's handler call.
pub layout InputOutcome: u8 tags {
    Running = 0
    Returned = 1
    Trapped = 2
} InputOutcome

/// An input of an instance: its header, the moniker of its sender, none for the core, and the name of its operation, or of the system interface its call reached, none when its handler call ended before telling it.
pub closed struct Input {
    pub header: InputHeader
    pub sender: Option[ident::Moniker]
    pub operation: Option[text::String]
} Input
